    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here's a draft rejection email that balances professionalism with kindness:\n\nDear [Candidate Name],\n\nI wanted to personally reach out to you regarding the status of your application for the Senior Developer position at [Company Name]. We were truly impressed by your exceptional system design skills and your alignment with our company culture, which made you a strong contender for the role.\n\nAfter careful consideration, we have decided to move forward with another candidate whose experience with our specific cloud stack aligns more closely with our current needs. Please know that this decision was not made lightly, and we were genuinely excited about the potential you brought to the table.\n\nI want to emphasize that your skills and experience are highly valued, and we would be delighted to have you consider other opportunities within our organization that may be a better fit. We also appreciate the time and effort you invested in our hiring process, and we're grateful for the opportunity to have met you.\n\nThank you again for your interest in joining our team, and we wish you the best of luck in your ongoing job search.\n\nBest regards,\n[Your Name]\n\nThis email aims to be kind and professional while still conveying the reasons for the rejection. It also leaves the door open for potential future opportunities, which is a nice way to maintain a",
